§483.450(b)(1)(iv)(D) The application of painful or noxious stimuli;
Guidance §483.450(b)(1)(iv)(D)
"Application of painful or noxious stimuli" is defined as any procedure by which staff apply,
contingent upon the exhibition of maladaptive behavior, startling, unpleasant, or painful stimuli,
or stimuli that have a potentially noxious effect.

